# Worksheet

**F1 Core loop** — `Game` state object; `mulberry32(seed)` rng used everywhere (terrain, colonists, events, storms, trade); `endTurn()` runs storm→consumption→morale→produce→events→trade→decay→win/lose in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map** — 8x8 `this.map` loop; `generateTerrain(rng,x,y)` seed-derived; `canBuild()` checks `building.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; adjacency dx/dy loop multiplies `produce` for GENERATOR/CONDENSER. Score 2.

**F3 Economy** — FORGE/GREENHOUSE `conversions` arrays consumed in `produceResources` (ore→metal, ash→soil→food); total-resource overflow check drops resources above `storage_capacity`. Score 2.

**F4 Population** — colonists have `skills{}`, `fatigue`, `morale`, `job`; `skill_bonus = c.skills[building.skill]` read in `produceResources`; `fatigue` is only ever written, never read by any formula. Score 1.

**F5 Needs** — per-colonist food/water `-=1`; shortage sets `c.morale -= 5`; but `produceResources` never reads `c.morale`, so it doesn't affect output; passive morale/fatigue recovery exists. Score 1.

**F6 Research** — 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; `canResearch` enforces prereqs+cost; `doResearch` deducts cost but only applies a real effect for 4/8 ids (ore_refining/irrigation/power_grid one-time grants, shelter_tech ongoing); advanced_forge/soil_science/preservation/advanced_lab do nothing. Score 1.

**F7 Events** — 10 entries in `EVENTS`; `fireEvent()` does weighted pick with `cooldown_done`; 4 events have 2 outcomes with genuinely different state effects, but the outcome is chosen by `rng()`, never presented to the player as a choice. Score 1.

**F8 Trade** — `updateTradeState()` drifts `trade_supply` and factors `resources[res]>200`; `buyResource`/`sellResource` both work and are wired to buttons; no caravan stock limit exists anywhere. Score 1.

**F9 Hazard** — `ashstorm_timer` fires periodically; severity scales water loss only (not damage chance); `tile.building_health` degrades and `health_factor` lowers `produceResources` output; `shelter_tech` research reduces damage; no repair function exists anywhere in the file. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load** — `serialize()`/`Game.deserialize()` via JSON in a copyable textarea; `loadGame()` try/catch shows `alert('Failed to load: '+e.message)` on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions** — lose: `colonists.length===0`; win: `turn>=60 && pop>=12 && food>=20 && water>=20`, both reachable; `calculateScore()` combines pop/research/scrip/turn; `renderGameOverModal()` shows summary. Score 2.

**F12 UI** — `switchTab()` swaps content; log entries carry `entry.turn`; `keydown` handles Space/1-6; `@media (max-width:600px)` reflows layout; tooltips are static `title=` text (terrain/description), not computed-value breakdowns. Score 1.

**F13 Dev panel** — `runTests()` checks real invariants (morale range, skill range, prereqs enforced, save/load round-trip); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints a `state_hash`. Score 2.

**G1** — `doResearch` writes one-time resource bumps (`resources.ore+=5`) not a stored modifier; `produceResources` formula never reads `research_done` or any research effect. Chain absent. Score 0.

**G2** — shortage writes `c.morale -= 5` (real state change), but `produceResources` formula has no `morale` term at all, so labor output never drops. Final link missing entirely. Score 1.

**G3** — `triggerAshstorm` damages `tile.building_health`; `health_factor` in `produceResources` genuinely reduces output; but no repair function anywhere raises `building_health` back, so cost/recovery links are entirely absent. Score 1.

**G4** — `updateTradeState` drifts `trade_supply` via rng each caravan cycle and factors stockpile threshold; `trade_prices` read by `buyResource`/`sellResource` and rendered in Trade tab every relevant turn. Score 4.

**G5** — `equipment_malfunction`/`vent_hazard`/`morale_crisis` branches write different resource deltas (`parts` vs `power`, colonist morale vs food) via `outcome.effect(this)`, not just log text. Score 3.

